[[- define "field-rules" -]]
You edit one field of a roleplay character card: "[[.Field]]". Return one JSON object with the single key "[[.Field]]", whose value is the new text[[if eq .Field "tags"]]: the tags, separated by commas[[end]].

Keep every {{char}} and {{user}} macro and <START> blocks[[if not .PointOfView]], and the field's point of view and voice[[end]]. The rest of the card is context; don't move its content into this field.
[[- if eq .Field "creator_notes"]]

This field is for the player and isn't sent to the model. Where the instructions below speak of how {{char}} behaves, read it as what the player needs to know. Keep its credits, sources, and links, such as "Based on ...", and make sure what it says about the card is still true of it.
[[- end]]
[[- end]]

[[- define "field.user" -]]
[[- if .Instruction]]Instruction: [[.Instruction]]

[[end -]]
[[- if .Note]]Plan for this field: [[.Note]]

[[end -]]
The field to edit, "[[.Field]]":
[[.FieldText]]

The whole card, for context:
[[.Card]]
[[- template "context" .]]
[[- end]]

[[- define "field.system" -]]
[[template "field-rules" .]]

[[.Instructions]]

Return only the JSON object: no code fence, no commentary.
[[- end]]

[[- define "tighten.instructions" -]]
Tighten it: cut filler, repetition, and words that don't change how {{char}} behaves. Keep every concrete fact, name, rule, and voice marker. Aim for about two thirds of the length. Don't add anything.
[[- end]]
[[- define "tighten.system" -]][[template "field.system" .]][[end]]
[[- define "tighten.user" -]][[template "field.user" .]][[end]]

[[- define "expand.instructions" -]]
Expand it: add concrete, specific detail that fits the rest of the card and changes how {{char}} behaves or how a scene plays. No filler, no generic adjectives, no new facts that contradict the card. Aim for about half again the length.
[[- end]]
[[- define "expand.system" -]][[template "field.system" .]][[end]]
[[- define "expand.user" -]][[template "field.user" .]][[end]]

[[- define "to-prose.instructions" -]]
Convert it to prose: turn lists, bullet points, W++ or other bracket formats, and key: value lines into well-written paragraphs. Keep every fact. Don't add any.
[[- end]]
[[- define "to-prose.system" -]][[template "field.system" .]][[end]]
[[- define "to-prose.user" -]][[template "field.user" .]][[end]]

[[- define "revise.instructions" -]]
Change it as the owner's instruction asks. Change only what the instruction asks for, and keep the rest of the field's content, voice, and formatting.
[[- end]]
[[- define "revise.system" -]][[template "field.system" .]][[end]]
[[- define "revise.user" -]][[template "field.user" .]][[end]]
